='white-space:nowrap;text-align:left;'></td><td style='white-space:nowrap;text-align:left;'></td><td style='white-space:nowrap;text-align:left;'>WHILE CLIMBING TO EN ROUTE CRUISING ALTITUDE OF FL190, CABIN DOOR ANNUNCIATOR ILLUMINATED AT APPROXIMATELY 18,700 FT.  EXECUTED EMERGENCY DESCENT AND "CABIN DOOR UNLOCK" EMERGENCY PROCEDURES.  AT 9000 MSL CABIN DOOR ANNUNCIATOR EXTINGUISHED.  AIRCRAFT LANDED UNEVENTFULLY.  INSPECTION OF DOOR AFTER LANDING INDICATED IT WAS SECURELY LATCHED.  MAINTENANCE FOUND UPPER AFT DOOR SWITCH OUT OF ADJUSTMENT.  ADJUSTED AFT DOOR SWITCH.  PRESSURIZED AIRCRAFT TO 6 PSI.  DOOR WARNING SYSTEM CHECKED SAT.</td></tr>
